from pathlib import Path
import json, html
p=Path(__file__).parent
v=json.loads((p/'validation.json').read_text()); preservation=json.loads((p/'preservation.json').read_text())
escape=html.escape
fmt=lambda n: f'{n:.3f}' if isinstance(n,(int,float)) else '—'
rows=''
for r in v['rows']:
 ab=r['abandonment']; rec=r['receive']; states=' → '.join(dict.fromkeys(t['feasibility'] for t in r['transitions'] if t.get('feasibility')))
 result=f"Receive at {fmt(rec['time'])} s · {fmt(rec['speedBefore'])} m/s" if rec and rec['executed'] else f"Abandon at {fmt(ab['time'])} s" if ab else r['outcome']
 rows+=f"<tr><td><a href='./?scenario={escape(r['id'])}'>{escape(r['label'])} ↗</a></td><td>{escape(str(r['selected']))}</td><td>{escape(states)}</td><td>{escape(result)}</td><td>{escape(ab['reason'] if ab else 'Run stays available until physical receive or observation ends.')}</td></tr>"
focusedpath=p/'focused-results.json';focused=json.loads(focusedpath.read_text()) if focusedpath.exists() else None
report=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Through Ball run release · provisional review</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"></head><body><header class="report"><div><div class="eyebrow">TOUCHLINE / THROUGH-TARGET-1 <span class="badge">PROVISIONAL · NOT FROZEN</span></div><h1>Attack the chance. Recognize when it’s gone.</h1><p>The same physical pass and initial runner selection, with ongoing feasibility and a visible release of the chase.</p></div></header><main class="report"><p><a href='./'>Open the playable review ↗</a> · <a href='../through-target-1/'>Previous runner lab</a> · <a href='../passing-v1-approved/passing/?setup=unified'>Frozen PASSING-V1</a></p><section class="card"><h2>What to watch</h2><p>Start with the terrible pass. The runner commits at full sprint, reacts toward the actual error, then releases the special run after sustained infeasibility. The coral dashed trail shows neutral recovery/deceleration. It is explicitly a lab placeholder for the normal AI handoff; no tactical team AI or runner reassignment has been added.</p><p>Then compare the easy, difficult and marginal cases. “Marginal” keeps the runner fighting. Passing errors stay on the physical ball throughout.</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Cases and actual outcomes</h2><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Runner</th><th>Feasibility states</th><th>Observed outcome</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table></div><p class="hint">Each link opens the same playable candidate with the named fixed fixture. Play, pause or scrub to inspect current ball, meeting, arrival times, deficit and commitment. All figures use seconds and metres.</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Exact provisional policy</h2><div id="policyNotes"><p>Every 0.15 s, search the authoritative ball’s remaining trajectory through physical rest or the moment the whole ball crosses the pitch boundary. Use the selected runner’s current velocity and heading, sprint capability, acceleration, braking and turn limit. The existing full-sprint movement planner supplies concrete meeting evidence.</p><p>Arrival times refer to the candidate future ball state, including availability after it stops. The displayed earliest-arrival estimate is deliberately optimistic: it integrates forward progress at 120 Hz under the existing movement limits, without charging lateral-path error. It is an estimate for filtering hopeless runs, not a guarantee that the runner can execute that path. A concrete feasible meeting inside the useful receive window keeps the chase alive.</p><p><b>REACHABLE:</b> earliest arrival has at least 0.25 s of spare time. <b>MARGINAL:</b> the deficit is no more than 0.65 s, or a concrete moving meeting remains possible. Marginal runners keep sprinting. Larger deficits with no verified meeting are <b>UNREACHABLE</b>. An unfinished forecast remains marginal rather than being treated as proof of failure.</p><p><b>Abandonment:</b> at least 0.60 s initial commitment, four consecutive unreachable assessments and at least 0.45 s of sustained infeasibility. Any reachable or marginal assessment resets this count. Once released, the run cannot reacquire ownership in this experiment.</p><p><b>Useful-through-ball window:</b> physical rest + 1.50 s, with a 0.25 s receive allowance (1.75 s total), anchored to the predicted rest time rather than moving forward on every replan. With no defenders, every inbounds stopped ball can eventually be fetched; this provisional rule separates a useful through-ball opportunity from later loose-ball retrieval. The allowance never extends a pitch exit. Eventual retrieval time is reported separately in the exact diagnostics. This timing policy remains open for owner review.</p><p><b>After release:</b> the runner decelerates along the current velocity at the unchanged Agility braking limit. Position and velocity remain continuous. The ball continues its authoritative simulation. This is the labelled neutral recovery placeholder, not tactical AI.</p><p>The standing player’s facing adds no invented startup delay: the unchanged movement controller can accelerate while body yaw aligns. The local pitch is 105 × 68 m: x −20 to 85, z −34 to 34. A ball is out only once its whole 0.11 m radius clears the boundary. Scenario-specific pitch placement is shown in diagnostics.</p></div><details><summary>All numerical rules</summary><pre>{escape(json.dumps(v['rules'],indent=2))}</pre></details></section><section class="card"><h2>Verification</h2><p>{v['checks']['passed']} independent candidate checks passed: exact deterministic repeats, unchanged initial selection, endpoint, launch and execution draws, physical continuity, full sprint while committed, irreversible release, deceleration and no reassignment.</p><p>{focused['passed'] if focused else '—'} focused behavioral checks also pass, including the nine requested scenarios, heading, momentum, acceleration and sprint capability. The same terrible-pass intent and runner setup receives at {fmt(focused['accurateTerribleControl']['receiveTime']) if focused else '—'} s with accurate execution; the bad execution keeps its physical error and loses the chance.</p><p>Preservation: <b>{escape(preservation['status'])}</b>. {preservation['passingFiles']} frozen passing files, {preservation['protectedLabFiles']} prior lab files, {preservation['productionFiles']} production files and {preservation.get('receiveFoundationFiles',35)} RECEIVE dependency files remain unchanged. Frozen tag <code>{escape(preservation['tag'])}</code>, commit <code>{escape(preservation['freezeCommit'])}</code>.</p><p><a href='validation.json'>Candidate checks and measurements</a> · <a href='focused-results.json'>Focused behavioral tests</a> · <a href='preservation.json'>Preservation audit</a></p><details><summary>Scope and limitations</summary><p>Reachability is a bounded numerical search under the current movement controller, not a proof of a globally optimal run. The neutral recovery placeholder decelerates naturally but does not make a tactical decision. There are no opponents, offside decisions, collisions between players or automatic ownership transfers.</p><p>The unchanged RECEIVE continuation uses its original BALL-FEEL-1.3 predictor, while the authoritative ball and pre-contact prediction remain frozen PASSING BALL-FEEL-1.4. This work does not tune receiving technique or the ball.</p></details></section></main><footer class="report">Ready for owner review. THROUGH-TARGET-1 remains provisional.</footer></body></html>'''
(p/'report.html').write_text(report)
print('report.html written')
